{:edb/db-before-t 1727 :edb/db-after-t 1728 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535040 50 #inst "2026-10-08T15:29:17.771Z" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328320 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328321 13194139535040 false] [17592186328320 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328383 13194139535040 true] [17592186328320 1145 "The function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{1+x^2y^2}$ is continuous on the rectangle $D=[0,\\sqrt2]\\times[-\\sqrt3,2]$. Fubini's theorem gives both I and II directly.\n\nIn III, the intervals are assigned to the opposite coordinate variables. Its region is the reflected rectangle $D^*=[-\\sqrt3,2]\\times[0,\\sqrt2]$, rather than $D$. Nevertheless, the integral has the same value: set $u=y$ and $v=x$, whose absolute Jacobian is $1$. Because $f(v,u)=f(u,v)$,\n\n$$\\int_{-\\sqrt3}^{2}\\int_0^{\\sqrt2}\\sqrt{1+x^2y^2}\\,dy\\,dx\n=\\int_{-\\sqrt3}^{2}\\int_0^{\\sqrt2}\\sqrt{1+u^2v^2}\\,du\\,dv\n=\\iint_D\\sqrt{1+x^2y^2}\\,dA.$$\n\nThus I, II, and III are all true. The original source's answer \"I and II only\" identifies the two expressions whose bounds directly match the stated coordinates, but omits the equal value in III due to symmetry. The study answer is \"I, II, and III\"." 13194139535040 true] [17592186328320 1145 "We notice that:  \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $\\sqrt{2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-\\sqrt{3}$ to $2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139535040 false] [17592186328383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328384 13194139535040 true] [17592186328383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328385 13194139535040 true] [17592186328383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328386 13194139535040 true] [17592186328383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328387 13194139535040 true] [17592186328383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328388 13194139535040 true] [17592186328383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328389 13194139535040 true] [17592186328383 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535040 true] [17592186328383 1041 "selection" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328383 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328389 13194139535040 true] [17592186328383 1110 #uuid "249bca12-e7c7-588f-b659-2eefa1ac3328" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328384 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328384 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535040 true] [17592186328384 1111 #uuid "aa2df4a4-9d68-50c5-93b4-4362e410abfa" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328385 1034 "III only" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328385 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535040 true] [17592186328385 1111 #uuid "6977f932-8bbd-5482-904c-e56c872e0e77" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328386 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328386 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535040 true] [17592186328386 1111 #uuid "58fcff74-31d5-58ac-9115-1a0243db96d8" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328387 1034 "I only" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328387 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535040 true] [17592186328387 1111 #uuid "1968c1ef-acfc-5ef1-b819-6fa362a27198" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328388 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328388 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535040 true] [17592186328388 1111 #uuid "cd859160-7d0d-5fba-a943-39d5596dcb50" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328389 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535040 true] [17592186328389 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535040 true] [17592186328389 1111 #uuid "d74ba33f-b4d1-598e-a9f9-7316815deed9" 13194139535040 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-72175/mathematical-correction-v1/selection" 17592186328383 "q-72175/mathematical-correction-v1/selection/answer-0" 17592186328384 "q-72175/mathematical-co